ication/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0010\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"non-colour cues\",\"reduced motion values\",\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and await numeric design decisions\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0011\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0011\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"missing provenance rejected\",\"human creative review recorded\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0012\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\",\"R0006\",\"R0008\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0012\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0006\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"all foundation ownership/dependencies/gates cross-checked\",\"does not claim release readiness\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this documentation contract\"}\n+  ]\n+}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..67c2b365c55b72b925528a14e78c3f710700d90e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+# Runbook-authoring allocation ledger\n+\n+This readable companion to [`runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](runbook-authoring-manifest.json) is the persistent allocation ledger for the mock-fantasy-quest-4 authoring system. The JSON is authoritative for IDs, provenance, dependencies, output paths, counters, and recovery state. Accepted IDs are immutable: resume from the first non-accepted batch and append only at `B0007` and `R0013`.\n+\n+## Wave 1 \u2014 foundation contracts\n+\n+| Order | Batch | R contracts (maximum 7) | Dependency / parallel disposition | Checkpoint |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| 1 | B0001 | R0001 | GATE-0001; no parallel work | Record gate and R0001 ownership |\n+| 2 | B0002 | R0002, R0003, R0010 | After B0001 | Validate seams, fixtures, tokens and retained gates |\n+| 3 | B0003 | R0004, R0008 | After B0002 | Validate state slice and P0 service exclusion |\n+| 4 | B0004 | R0005, R0006 | After B0003; R0006 waits for GATE-0003 | Validate content/save separation |\n+| 5 | B0005 | R0007, R0009, R0011 | After B0004; R0007/GATE-0003 and R0009/GATE-0005 remain blocked | Validate migration, diagnostics, provenance |\n+| 6 | B0006 | R0012 | After B0003 and B0004; safe in parallel with B0005 after B0004 | Cross-check foundation documentation and gates |\n+\n+The batches are deliberately smaller than seven where a contract is context-heavy (state, persistence, content) or tightly coupled to its predecessor. Together they form an incremental foundation vertical slice: reproducible baseline, shared seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery boundaries, then provenance/diagnostic controls and documented closure. They do not imply that the game is implemented.\n+\n+## Contract allocation and asset assessment\n+\n+| R ID | IMP source | Writer | Output | Asset assessment |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| R0001 | IMP-0001 | B0001 | `runbooks/R0001.md` | not applicable \u2014 tooling boundary only |\n+| R0002 | IMP-0002 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0002.md` | not applicable \u2014 interfaces only |\n+| R0003 | IMP-0003 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0003.md` | not applicable \u2014 deterministic fixtures only |\n+| R0004 | IMP-0004 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0004.md` | not applicable \u2014 state envelopes only |\n+| R0005 | IMP-0005 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0005.md` | not applicable \u2014 schema reserves later asset fields |\n+| R0006 | IMP-0006 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0006.md` | not applicable \u2014 save/recovery protocol |\n+| R0007 | IMP-0007 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0007.md` | not applicable \u2014 migrations only |\n+| R0008 | IMP-0008 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0008.md` | not applicable \u2014 negative service scope |\n+| R0009 | IMP-0009 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0009.md` | not applicable \u2014 local diagnostics only |\n+| R0010 | IMP-0010 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0010.md` | not applicable \u2014 no final art/fonts/icons |\n+| R0011 | IMP-0011 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0011.md` | not applicable \u2014 provenance control only |\n+| R0012 | IMP-0012 | B0006 | `runbooks/R0012.md` | not applicable \u2014 documentation only |\n+\n+No Wave 1 contract creates a product asset. Each contract still carries an explicit `asset_impact`, empty `asset_ids`, and an asset brief in the JSON; its author must prohibit incidental asset creation. A later asset-required contract must reserve stable product-specific IDs and a brief before assignment.\n+\n+## Author packet and resume rules\n+\n+Each B writer receives only the baseline terminology, target constraints, templates, authoring rules, and the named specification/catalogue records in its JSON `context_packet`. Every R record has canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`, and `factory_stages` provenance. Use [`runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`](../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md) plus the F014 metadata and asset requirements.\n+\n+At every checkpoint, validate unique B/R IDs, output-path ownership, dependency closure, provenance, the batch maximum, asset assessment, and retained human gates. On failure, retain all assigned IDs, repair the bounded failed output, and resume that same batch. Never regenerate accepted contracts or renumber the ledger.\n+\n+## Queued expansion chapters\n+\n+| Chapter | Future allocation point | State |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| SHARD-02 \u2014 Campaign content and domain logic | Wave 2 after GATE-0004 | queued |\n+| SHARD-03 \u2014 Session, UI, input, and accessibility | Wave 3 after SHARD-02 and GATE-0002/0003/0004 | queued |\n+| SHARD-04 \u2014 PWA delivery, performance, operations, release evidence | Wave 4 after SHARD-02/03 and GATE-0002/0005/0007 | queued |\n+| SHARD-05 \u2014 Connected-scope decision package | Only explicit authorisation after GATE-0006; no P0 R allocation | hold |\n+\n+Expand one queued chapter into catalogue records before allocating its R IDs. This preserves the catalogue\u2019s dependency graph and makes a future thousand-runbook programme resumable without changing accepted work.\n+\n+## Structural check\n+\n+```sh\n+node -e 'const m=require(\"./projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"); const r=m.r_contracts, b=m.batches, ids=a=>new Set(a).size===a.length; if (!ids(r.map(x=>x.id)) || !ids(b.map(x=>x.id)) || r.length!==m.expected_runbook_count || b.some(x=>x.r_contract_ids.length>7) || r.some(x=>!x.source_specifications.length || !x.source_catalogue_ids.length || !x.authoring_batch || !x.factory_stages.length || ![\"required\",\"not_applicable\"].includes(x.asset_impact) || !x.output_path || (x.asset_impact===\"required\" && (!x.asset_ids.length || !x.asset_brief))) ) process.exit(1); console.log(\"runbook authoring ledger structural check passed\")'\n+```\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..54c73f01829d105454656a3b544dfccaeae8654f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+{\n+  \"manifest_id\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4-runbook-authoring-ledger\",\n+  \"version\": 1,\n+  \"purpose\": \"Persistent, append-only allocation ledger for bounded B-series authoring batches and immutable R-series implementation contracts. It allocates the current catalogue only; queued shards remain expansion work.\",\n+  \"project_slug\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4\",\n+  \"source_catalogue\": \"planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\n+  \"expected_runbook_count\": 12,\n+  \"id_counters\": {\"next_authoring_batch_id\": \"B0007\", \"next_implementation_runbook_id\": \"R0013\", \"rule\": \"Never reuse, renumber, or replace an accepted B or R ID. Append new allocations using these counters only.\"},\n+  \"wave\": {\"number\": 1, \"state\": \"planned\", \"checkpoint_after_each_batch\": true, \"resume_from\": \"first batch whose state is not accepted; validate accepted IDs, paths, and provenance before dispatch\", \"recovery\": \"If a batch fails, retain its IDs, mark it blocked or repairable, repair only its listed output paths, validate its contracts, then resume that same batch. Do not reallocate its R IDs.\"},\n+  \"catalogue_disposition\": {\"allocated\": [\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\"], \"deferred\": [], \"human_gates_retained\": {\"IMP-0001\":\"GATE-0001\", \"IMP-0006\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0007\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0009\":\"GATE-0005\", \"IMP-0010\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004\"}},\n+  \"queued_expansion\": [\n+    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 2 after GATE-0004\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand into bounded IMP records before assigning any R IDs\"},\n+    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-03\",\"title\":\"Session, UI, input, and accessibility\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 3 after GATE-0002,GATE-0003,GATE-0004\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand after its predecessor shards; preserve shared UI and web-adapter ownership\"},\n+    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-04\",\"title\":\"PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 4 after GATE-0002,GATE-0005,GATE-0007\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand only after the session/UI and campaign contracts exist\"},\n+    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-05\",\"title\":\"Connected-scope decision package\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"state\":\"hold\",\"future_wave\":\"only if explicitly authorised after GATE-0006\",\"allocation_rule\":\"no P0 implementation R contracts\"}\n+  ],\n+  \"context_packet_baseline\": {\n+    \"terminology\": [\"B-series = authoring runbook\", \"R-series = generated implementation runbook\", \"IMP-series = catalogue contract\", \"shared core\", \"web adapter\", \"PWA delivery adapter\", \"local save\", \"cache\", \"human gate\"],\n+    \"target_constraints\": [\"original offline-capable 2D single-player RPG\", \"responsive web and installable PWA\", \"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad\", \"no accounts, sync, multiplayer, purchases, or network services in P0\", \"shared core must not import platform/render/network modules\", \"PWA cache and save data remain separate\"],\n+    \"required_templates\": [\"runbooks/TEMPLATE.md\", \"runbooks/F014.md provenance and asset-assessment requirements\"],\n+    \"authoring_rules\": [\"write only assigned paths\", \"preserve gates and unanswered questions\", \"do not create incidental assets when asset_impact is not_applicable\", \"perform structural, not product-release, validation\"]\n+  },\n+  \"batches\": [\n+    {\"id\":\"B0001\",\"order\":1,\"title\":\"Bootstrap decision-gated foundation\",\"state\":\"blocked_on_gate\",\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 framework, package manager, and CI selection\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0001\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/platform-appendix.md\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0001\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate R0001 metadata and output ownership, record gate disposition, then checkpoint wave\",\"recovery\":\"keep R0001 reserved; after the gate, rerun B0001 only\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"one bounded R runbook\",\"gate is explicit\",\"baseline command and ownership evidence are specified\"]},\n+    {\"id\":\"B0002\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"Shared seams, deterministic harness, and token contract\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0001\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0001 accepted; R0012's visual-token portion remains blocked by GATE-0002,GATE-0004\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0010\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0010\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate the three contracts and record any gate-blocked subwork\",\"recovery\":\"repair only R0002,R0003,R0010; never split or renumber accepted contracts\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"core/adapter seam precedes feature work\",\"fixture and token outputs have distinct ownership\",\"all gates retained\"]},\n+    {\"id\":\"B0003\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"Deterministic state slice and connected-scope exclusion\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0002\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0002 accepted\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0004\",\"R0008\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0008\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate state/event ownership and negative connected-scope coverage\",\"recovery\":\"retain IDs and repair the failed R contract only\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"vertical foundation slice remains independently reviewable\",\"P0 connected-service exclusion is explicit\"]},\n+    {\"id\":\"B0004\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"Content validation and local recovery protocols\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0003 accepted; R0006 requires GATE-0003\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate content/save boundaries and retained storage gate\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0005,R0006 and rerun the blocked item after its decision\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"content and save/cache ownership is separated\",\"save recovery remains a bounded foundation slice\"]},\n+    {\"id\":\"B0005\",\"order\":5,\"title\":\"Migration, diagnostics, and provenance controls\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0006 after B0004 acceptance, except R0007 still waits for R0006\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0007 needs GATE-0003; R0009 needs GATE-0005\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0007\",\"R0009\",\"R0011\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0011\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate migration, diagnostics, and provenance fields; record unresolved gates\",\"recovery\":\"rerun only incomplete assigned IDs; preserve any accepted R contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no transport or remote diagnostics is introduced\",\"provenance review is explicit\",\"contracts remain at most three\"]},\n+    {\"id\":\"B0006\",\"order\":6,\"title\":\"Foundation documentation closure\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\",\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0005 after B0004 acceptance\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0006 must be accepted or documented as blocked; no gate is implicitly resolved\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0012\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0012\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"cross-check all foundation ownership, dependencies, and gates before accepting the wave\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0012 and correct only its documentation contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documentation concludes the foundation slice without claiming implementation or approval\",\"gated save work remains visible\"]}\n+  ],\n+  \"r_contracts\": [\n+    {\"id\":\"R0001\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0001\",\"title\":\"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\"dependencies\":[],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0001\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0001\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No product asset work; establish only project/tooling boundaries and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documented deterministic baseline command\",\"isolated ownership directories\",\"GATE-0001 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and path; repair only this contract\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0002\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0002\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0002.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#dependency-direction-and-state-rules\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0002\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; this is an interface and dependency-policy contract.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"forbidden core imports rejected\",\"adapter command-only fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0003\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#observability-quality-evidence-and-release-verification\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0003\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; fixtures use non-product deterministic data.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"repeatable fixture result\",\"isolated fixture storage\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0004\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0004\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; state envelopes deliberately exclude authored content.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"stale and invalid commands do not mutate state\",\"duplicate interaction is idempotent\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0005\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No art/audio assets; reserve only schema/provenance fields for later original assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"valid minimal package passes\",\"invalid references fail\",\"reachability fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0006\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0006\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; protocol is data/recovery only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"fault fixtures cover write and validation failures\",\"save/cache separation\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID; wait for storage decision before accepting gated work\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0007\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0007\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; migration fixtures retain original bytes only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"predecessors migrate once\",\"failed candidate remains intact\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and resume after R0006/gate closure\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0008\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0008\",\"title\":\"Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0008\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; a negative scope boundary.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no identity/token/network fields\",\"future connected work remains gated\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0009\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0009\",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0009\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; local redacted records only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"consent and deletion controls\",\"payload redaction\",\"no network transport\",\"GATE-0005 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and wait for privacy gate where required\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0010\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0010\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"non-colour cues\",\"reduced motion values\",\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and await numeric design decisions\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0011\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0011\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"missing provenance rejected\",\"human creative review recorded\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0012\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\",\"R0006\",\"R0008\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0012\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0006\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"all foundation ownership/dependencies/gates cross-checked\",\"does not claim release readiness\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this documentation contract\"}\n+  ]\n+}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..67c2b365c55b72b925528a14e78c3f710700d90e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+# Runbook-authoring allocation ledger\n+\n+This readable companion to [`runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](runbook-authoring-manifest.json) is the persistent allocation ledger for the mock-fantasy-quest-4 authoring system. The JSON is authoritative for IDs, provenance, dependencies, output paths, counters, and recovery state. Accepted IDs are immutable: resume from the first non-accepted batch and append only at `B0007` and `R0013`.\n+\n+## Wave 1 \u2014 foundation contracts\n+\n+| Order | Batch | R contracts (maximum 7) | Dependency / parallel disposition | Checkpoint |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| 1 | B0001 | R0001 | GATE-0001; no parallel work | Record gate and R0001 ownership |\n+| 2 | B0002 | R0002, R0003, R0010 | After B0001 | Validate seams, fixtures, tokens and retained gates |\n+| 3 | B0003 | R0004, R0008 | After B0002 | Validate state slice and P0 service exclusion |\n+| 4 | B0004 | R0005, R0006 | After B0003; R0006 waits for GATE-0003 | Validate content/save separation |\n+| 5 | B0005 | R0007, R0009, R0011 | After B0004; R0007/GATE-0003 and R0009/GATE-0005 remain blocked | Validate migration, diagnostics, provenance |\n+| 6 | B0006 | R0012 | After B0003 and B0004; safe in parallel with B0005 after B0004 | Cross-check foundation documentation and gates |\n+\n+The batches are deliberately smaller than seven where a contract is context-heavy (state, persistence, content) or tightly coupled to its predecessor. Together they form an incremental foundation vertical slice: reproducible baseline, shared seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery boundaries, then provenance/diagnostic controls and documented closure. They do not imply that the game is implemented.\n+\n+## Contract allocation and asset assessment\n+\n+| R ID | IMP source | Writer | Output | Asset assessment |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| R0001 | IMP-0001 | B0001 | `runbooks/R0001.md` | not applicable \u2014 tooling boundary only |\n+| R0002 | IMP-0002 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0002.md` | not applicable \u2014 interfaces only |\n+| R0003 | IMP-0003 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0003.md` | not applicable \u2014 deterministic fixtures only |\n+| R0004 | IMP-0004 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0004.md` | not applicable \u2014 state envelopes only |\n+| R0005 | IMP-0005 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0005.md` | not applicable \u2014 schema reserves later asset fields |\n+| R0006 | IMP-0006 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0006.md` | not applicable \u2014 save/recovery protocol |\n+| R0007 | IMP-0007 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0007.md` | not applicable \u2014 migrations only |\n+| R0008 | IMP-0008 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0008.md` | not applicable \u2014 negative service scope |\n+| R0009 | IMP-0009 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0009.md` | not applicable \u2014 local diagnostics only |\n+| R0010 | IMP-0010 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0010.md` | not applicable \u2014 no final art/fonts/icons |\n+| R0011 | IMP-0011 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0011.md` | not applicable \u2014 provenance control only |\n+| R0012 | IMP-0012 | B0006 | `runbooks/R0012.md` | not applicable \u2014 documentation only |\n+\n+No Wave 1 contract creates a product asset. Each contract still carries an explicit `asset_impact`, empty `asset_ids`, and an asset brief in the JSON; its author must prohibit incidental asset creation. A later asset-required contract must reserve stable product-specific IDs and a brief before assignment.\n+\n+## Author packet and resume rules\n+\n+Each B writer receives only the baseline terminology, target constraints, templates, authoring rules, and the named specification/catalogue records in its JSON `context_packet`. Every R record has canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`, and `factory_stages` provenance. Use [`runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`](../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md) plus the F014 metadata and asset requirements.\n+\n+At every checkpoint, validate unique B/R IDs, output-path ownership, dependency closure, provenance, the batch maximum, asset assessment, and retained human gates. On failure, retain all assigned IDs, repair the bounded failed output, and resume that same batch. Never regenerate accepted contracts or renumber the ledger.\n+\n+## Queued expansion chapters\n+\n+| Chapter | Future allocation point | State |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| SHARD-02 \u2014 Campaign content and domain logic | Wave 2 after GATE-0004 | queued |\n+| SHARD-03 \u2014 Session, UI, input, and accessibility | Wave 3 after SHARD-02 and GATE-0002/0003/0004 | queued |\n+| SHARD-04 \u2014 PWA delivery, performance, operations, release evidence | Wave 4 after SHARD-02/03 and GATE-0002/0005/0007 | queued |\n+| SHARD-05 \u2014 Connected-scope decision package | Only explicit authorisation after GATE-0006; no P0 R allocation | hold |\n+\n+Expand one queued chapter into catalogue records before allocating its R IDs. This preserves the catalogue\u2019s dependency graph and makes a future thousand-runbook programme resumable without changing accepted work.\n+\n+## Structural check\n+\n+```sh\n+node -e 'const m=require(\"./projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"); const r=m.r_contracts, b=m.batches, ids=a=>new Set(a).size===a.length; if (!ids(r.map(x=>x.id)) || !ids(b.map(x=>x.id)) || r.length!==m.expected_runbook_count || b.some(x=>x.r_contract_ids.length>7) || r.some(x=>!x.source_specifications.length || !x.source_catalogue_ids.length || !x.authoring_batch || !x.factory_stages.length || ![\"required\",\"not_applicable\"].includes(x.asset_impact) || !x.output_path || (x.asset_impact===\"required\" && (!x.asset_ids.length || !x.asset_brief))) ) process.exit(1); console.log(\"runbook authoring ledger structural check passed\")'\n+```\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Created the Wave 1 allocation ledger with si