kpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and wait for privacy gate where required\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0010\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0010\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"non-colour cues\",\"reduced motion values\",\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and await numeric design decisions\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0011\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0011\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"missing provenance rejected\",\"human creative review recorded\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n+    {\"id\":\"R0012\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\",\"R0006\",\"R0008\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0012\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0006\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"all foundation ownership/dependencies/gates cross-checked\",\"does not claim release readiness\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this documentation contract\"}\n+  ]\n+}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..67c2b365c55b72b925528a14e78c3f710700d90e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+# Runbook-authoring allocation ledger\n+\n+This readable companion to [`runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](runbook-authoring-manifest.json) is the persistent allocation ledger for the mock-fantasy-quest-4 authoring system. The JSON is authoritative for IDs, provenance, dependencies, output paths, counters, and recovery state. Accepted IDs are immutable: resume from the first non-accepted batch and append only at `B0007` and `R0013`.\n+\n+## Wave 1 \u2014 foundation contracts\n+\n+| Order | Batch | R contracts (maximum 7) | Dependency / parallel disposition | Checkpoint |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| 1 | B0001 | R0001 | GATE-0001; no parallel work | Record gate and R0001 ownership |\n+| 2 | B0002 | R0002, R0003, R0010 | After B0001 | Validate seams, fixtures, tokens and retained gates |\n+| 3 | B0003 | R0004, R0008 | After B0002 | Validate state slice and P0 service exclusion |\n+| 4 | B0004 | R0005, R0006 | After B0003; R0006 waits for GATE-0003 | Validate content/save separation |\n+| 5 | B0005 | R0007, R0009, R0011 | After B0004; R0007/GATE-0003 and R0009/GATE-0005 remain blocked | Validate migration, diagnostics, provenance |\n+| 6 | B0006 | R0012 | After B0003 and B0004; safe in parallel with B0005 after B0004 | Cross-check foundation documentation and gates |\n+\n+The batches are deliberately smaller than seven where a contract is context-heavy (state, persistence, content) or tightly coupled to its predecessor. Together they form an incremental foundation vertical slice: reproducible baseline, shared seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery boundaries, then provenance/diagnostic controls and documented closure. They do not imply that the game is implemented.\n+\n+## Contract allocation and asset assessment\n+\n+| R ID | IMP source | Writer | Output | Asset assessment |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| R0001 | IMP-0001 | B0001 | `runbooks/R0001.md` | not applicable \u2014 tooling boundary only |\n+| R0002 | IMP-0002 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0002.md` | not applicable \u2014 interfaces only |\n+| R0003 | IMP-0003 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0003.md` | not applicable \u2014 deterministic fixtures only |\n+| R0004 | IMP-0004 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0004.md` | not applicable \u2014 state envelopes only |\n+| R0005 | IMP-0005 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0005.md` | not applicable \u2014 schema reserves later asset fields |\n+| R0006 | IMP-0006 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0006.md` | not applicable \u2014 save/recovery protocol |\n+| R0007 | IMP-0007 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0007.md` | not applicable \u2014 migrations only |\n+| R0008 | IMP-0008 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0008.md` | not applicable \u2014 negative service scope |\n+| R0009 | IMP-0009 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0009.md` | not applicable \u2014 local diagnostics only |\n+| R0010 | IMP-0010 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0010.md` | not applicable \u2014 no final art/fonts/icons |\n+| R0011 | IMP-0011 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0011.md` | not applicable \u2014 provenance control only |\n+| R0012 | IMP-0012 | B0006 | `runbooks/R0012.md` | not applicable \u2014 documentation only |\n+\n+No Wave 1 contract creates a product asset. Each contract still carries an explicit `asset_impact`, empty `asset_ids`, and an asset brief in the JSON; its author must prohibit incidental asset creation. A later asset-required contract must reserve stable product-specific IDs and a brief before assignment.\n+\n+## Author packet and resume rules\n+\n+Each B writer receives only the baseline terminology, target constraints, templates, authoring rules, and the named specification/catalogue records in its JSON `context_packet`. Every R record has canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`, and `factory_stages` provenance. Use [`runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`](../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md) plus the F014 metadata and asset requirements.\n+\n+At every checkpoint, validate unique B/R IDs, output-path ownership, dependency closure, provenance, the batch maximum, asset assessment, and retained human gates. On failure, retain all assigned IDs, repair the bounded failed output, and resume that same batch. Never regenerate accepted contracts or renumber the ledger.\n+\n+## Queued expansion chapters\n+\n+| Chapter | Future allocation point | State |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| SHARD-02 \u2014 Campaign content and domain logic | Wave 2 after GATE-0004 | queued |\n+| SHARD-03 \u2014 Session, UI, input, and accessibility | Wave 3 after SHARD-02 and GATE-0002/0003/0004 | queued |\n+| SHARD-04 \u2014 PWA delivery, performance, operations, release evidence | Wave 4 after SHARD-02/03 and GATE-0002/0005/0007 | queued |\n+| SHARD-05 \u2014 Connected-scope decision package | Only explicit authorisation after GATE-0006; no P0 R allocation | hold |\n+\n+Expand one queued chapter into catalogue records before allocating its R IDs. This preserves the catalogue\u2019s dependency graph and makes a future thousand-runbook programme resumable without changing accepted work.\n+\n+## Structural check\n+\n+```sh\n+node -e 'const m=require(\"./projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"); const r=m.r_contracts, b=m.batches, ids=a=>new Set(a).size===a.length; if (!ids(r.map(x=>x.id)) || !ids(b.map(x=>x.id)) || r.length!==m.expected_runbook_count || b.some(x=>x.r_contract_ids.length>7) || r.some(x=>!x.source_specifications.length || !x.source_catalogue_ids.length || !x.authoring_batch || !x.factory_stages.length || ![\"required\",\"not_applicable\"].includes(x.asset_impact) || !x.output_path || (x.asset_impact===\"required\" && (!x.asset_ids.length || !x.asset_brief))) ) process.exit(1); console.log(\"runbook authoring ledger structural check passed\")'\n+```\n\ntokens used\n51,368\n", "adapter_log": "", "test_log": "runbook authoring manifest comprehensive structural check passed\n git diff --check passed", "browser_log": "", "screenshots": []}, "acceptance_results": [{"criterion": "Every available `IMP-*` record belongs to exactly one batch or has a documented human gate/deferment; queued requirements identify their future expansion chapter. Every allocated `R-*` ID is unique and immutable.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "All 12 catalogue IMP records are allocated exactly once to R0001\u2013R0012 and their six B batches; retained human gates and SHARD-02\u201305 future waves are recorded. Immutable counter rules and next IDs are in the manifest."}, {"criterion": "Batch ordering respects the catalogue dependency graph and identifies batches safe to author in parallel versus those requiring a preceding decision.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Each R contract preserves its IMP prerequisites; B0001\u2013B0006 identify batch dependencies, gates, and the only safe B0005/B0006 parallel point."}, {"criterion": "Each batch has a context packet listing only the relevant specification, catalogue records, terminology, target constraints, required templates, and explicit provenance values for every allocated R contract: canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, originating `authoring_batch`, and the relevant `factory_stages`.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "The manifest has a constrained baseline context packet plus per-batch relevant specification and IMP record lists. Every R record includes all four required provenance fields."}, {"criterion": "No authoring batch is assigned more than seven R-series contracts; a smaller batch is required when its contracts are tightly coupled or context-heavy.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Batches contain 1, 3, 2, 2, 3, and 1 R contracts. The companion explains the deliberate smaller context-heavy/tightly coupled batches."}, {"criterion": "The manifest records expected runbook count, IDs, dependencies, output paths, acceptance checks, checkpoint cadence, recovery instructions, and an explicit asset assessment for every allocated R contract. The assessment records `asset_impact` as either `required` or `not_applicable`; asset-required contracts reserve stable, product-specific `asset_ids` and identify their asset brief/purpose before a B-series writer is assigned.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "All 12 R records include these fields. Wave 1 is foundation-only, so each assessment is explicitly not_applicable with an empty asset_ids array and asset brief prohibiting incidental assets."}, {"criterion": "Batches preserve end-to-end vertical slices as well as foundation work, so a large product can be implemented and reviewed incrementally.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "The ledger sequences baseline/seams/harness, deterministic state and service exclusion, content plus recovery, control/provenance work, and documentation closure as reviewable foundation slices."}, {"criterion": "The ledger contains monotonic next-ID counters and wave state, so a resumed dispatcher never renumbers accepted B-series or R-series work.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "id_counters reserve B0007 and R0013, and the wave state specifies checkpointing, immutable accepted IDs, bounded repair, and resume from the first non-accepted batch."}], "documentation": {"reviewed_files": ["projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md", "runbooks/TEMPLATE.md", "runbooks/F014.md", "runbooks/F015.md"], "updated_files": ["projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md"], "summary": "Added the required machine-readable ledger and its user-facing Markdown companion, including validation and safe-resume guidance."}, "known_limitations": [], "browser_coverage": "Not applicable: this is domain-only planning and documentation work; no browser behavior or Playwright specification changed.", "recommended_next_step": "complete"}


